.po 0
.ll 80
.ce 1
SLED Command Summary
.bl 2
.in 8
Command                 Action
-------                 --------------------------------------------
Up Arrow                Move up one line.
Down Arrow              Move down one line.
Right Arrow             Move right one character.
Left Arrow              Move left one character.
Shift-Up Arrow          Move back on screen page.
Shift-Down Arrow        Move forward one screen page.
Shift-Right Arrow       Tab to next Tab stop.
Shift-Left Arrow        Detab to previous Tab stop.
.bl 1
<ENTER>                 Start a new line.
.bl 1
Cntl - A                Add (or insert) a new line at cursor position.
Cntl - B                Go to the beginning of the text buffer.
Cntl - C                Clear to the end of the current line.
Cntl - D                Delete the character under the cursor.
Alt  - D                Change to a new directory.
Cntl - E                Go to the end of the text buffer.
Cntl - F                Alternate file read.
Cntl - G                Enter Global Command Processor.
Cntl - K                Delete the current line.
Alt  - M                Mark block of text.
Cntl - N                Insert a single SPACE at the cursor position.
Cntl - O                Alternate output.  Doesn't delete lines.
Cntl - P                Position the cursor to a text line.
Cntl - Q                Quit SLED
Cntl - R                Read an input file.
Cntl - S                Set the left margin at the cursor position.
Cntl - U                Update the text buffer.
Alt  - U                User interface to the Shell.
Cntl - V                Move to the next screen line.
Cntl - W                Write the buffer to a file deleting lines.
.bl 1
Alt -- H                Show Help screens.
.bl 1
F1                      Toggle Insert Mode On/Off.
F2                      Toggle Word-Wrap On/Off.
Shift-F1                Toggle Auto-Indent Mode On/Off.
.bl 1
<ESC>ape (Cntl-Break)   Abort a command in progress.
.bl 2
.ce 1
Global Commands
.bl 1
Command                 Action
-------                 --------------------------------------------
C                       Execute the copy of the marked block.
M                       Execute the move of the marked block.
K [#lines]              Kill block or #lines starting at cursor
                        position.
A #lines                Add #lines starting at cursor position.
F/string/#times         Find <string> #times
R/string1/string2/#     Replace <string1> with <string2> #times.

